ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Draft M37a — new JEE-relevant grounded-wire-current observable\n\n**Frozen charter BEFORE code:** `docs/m37a_charter.md` committed at `89dae06df53403a8fab6743ad8bdcc10fc76c514`.\n**Released base:** M36e merge `dc347251c14e449c53d51820b4481d1bfbee2cfb`, Git tree `60b4f21aa88a2031ec50c5d1e7c15a5135a7becf`, 20/20 real main-push CI passed.\n\nM37a adds **a new ideal quasistatic ground-wire current observer**, not a new 3D electrostatic solver or fake motion animation. Existing exact Kelvin ground-sphere and M13 force/energy are observed at each source position. A teacher-supplied instantaneous velocity gives only `I_sphere→ground=-q a v_radial/d²` (conventional positive-charge direction); true radial `I(t)` consumes actual M16a trajectories, verifies the full timeline against fresh M16a integration, and retains real elapsed time, energy, guard and source model. Signed induced charge `Q_sphere=-q a/d` is derived from the native physical solution. No wire resistance, EM delay, radiation or surface-contact dynamics.\n\n**Novel evidence:** independent SI force `F_r=-k q² a d/(d²-a²)²`, mechanical energy `U=-k q² a/[2(d²-a²)]`, native-position charge derivative `-dQ/dt`; positive/negative incoming/outgoing/tangential, translated and rotated geometry, permittivity, actual RK4 radial time series, near-surface guard, hostile false sign/charge/velocity/energy/time/provenance refusals. Independent stdlib JSON physics checker imports **no conductor_sim**. Dedicated Python 3.10/3.12 workflow plus full inherited CI required.\n\n**JEE fidelity:** the M36a audit lists physical p8 Multiple Correct Q21 in `02_conductors_half_size.pdf` as partial. No unreviewed claim of the problem's complete source wording/answer or numeric givens; this PR is a reusable *current observable* first. Original source page and answer need independent visual inspection in review.\n\n**DO NOT MERGE OR MARK READY** until current exact-head source CI (full Python 3.10/3.12, historical browser, real FEMM 5, new M37a physics), new fresh independent source-pinned reviewer math/browser-source checks, explicit owner authorization, exact-head merge and postmerge main-push CI. Unrelated physics/solver/renderer files remain unchanged.\n\nSee [M37a charter](docs/m37a_charter.md), [design + limits](docs/m37a.md), `src/conductor_sim/grounded_sphere_wire.py`, `tests/test_m37a_grounded_wire_current.py`, `tools/m37a_ground_wire_reference.py`, and `examples/grounded_sphere_wire_current.py`.\n\n\n### Independent review history and FINAL current F4 correction\n\n**Current exact candidate:** `630f6d320a1b4cb00bf7bb0780cd3deca4ec0f7e`; actual native Git TREE `796f319edf5829455e842d9bad63b770d17ff9fa`. All source code/FEMM/M16/current observer unchanged since R2; only stdlib export checker, focused adversarial tests and M37a documentation altered.\n\n- **Independent review #01** on old `75c984aa...`: [CHANGES REQUESTED](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/pull/6) on 11 Boolean/SI-unit/source-identity forgeries. Original first red evidence preserved.\n- **Independent review #02** on later `adfe9098...`: [CHANGES REQUESTED](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/pull/7). F1–F3 and Kelvin physics / actual M16a passed, but independent reviewer found **F4:** offline JSON checker accepted a fake maximum energy drift, negative physical approach guard and a spurious surface event during duration-complete motion. Its red original review workflow remains red.\n- **Current F4 corrections:** strict finite positive saved guard and sample clearance; max absolute energy drift checked against actual independently SI-verified saved sample drifts; event kind/time/position/physical-axis/chronology validated; duration runs forbid guard events and genuine guard terminations require a terminal event matching the actual final sample. Standalone JSON checks do not pretend to re-integrate the ODE or give cryptographic provenance.\n- **Developer-controlled current focused workflow:** 120 scientific/source/hostile tests passed **on both Python 3.10 and Python 3.12**, plus generated native example JSON and independent stdlib SI physics check. Full **exact HEAD** original Python, FEMM, Chromium and other PR/branch-push workflow runs must all reach terminal SUCCESS; older green SHA is not sufficient.\n- **One bounded independent re-review #03 required (not a new full physics review):** [REQUEST #03](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/blob/main/projects/conductor_sim/pr-89/REQUEST-03.md) and [REVIEWER PROMPT #03](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/blob/main/projects/conductor_sim/pr-89/REVIEWER-PROMPT-03.md). The SAME independent reviewer who found F4 may re-execute original attacks and unfamiliar event/guard falsifications; unchanged independently reviewed Kelvin and PDF code need not be re-reviewed from scratch.\n\nOriginal JEE workbook `02_conductors_half_size.pdf` p8 Multiple Correct Q21 says q>0 approaching grounded sphere at **externally prescribed constant small speed**, key **(1),(3)**, not freely accelerating M16a. Teacher numerical examples are not textbook numerical givens; no automatic whole-question coverage is claimed.\n\n**PR #89 is DRAFT AND UNMERGED. NO NEW INDEPENDENT PASS OR OWNER MERGE APPROVAL EXISTS.** After a genuine new PASS, obtain explicit owner approval, enforce `expected_head_sha`, compare actual merged Git tree, then require every actual postmerge main-push workflow SUCCESS.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-18T12:21:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T13:55:37Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1bfb047f48ed2d821854327d3387ec580b320fb6","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"physicsvigilante:m37a-grounded-sphere-wire-current","ref":"m37a-groun